WEBVTT

00:00:00.698 --> 00:00:02.603
Rhetorical synthesis.

00:00:02.603 --> 00:00:04.293
Read the goal first.

00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:05.494
The notes come last.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:09.009
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.524
A bulleted list of a student's notes.

00:00:11.524 --> 00:00:14.179
And a question that says: the student wants to.

00:00:15.193 --> 00:00:19.341
It's testing whether you can choose information to do one specific job.

00:00:20.402 --> 00:00:21.937
Here's the method.

00:00:21.937 --> 00:00:23.882
Read the question first.

00:00:23.882 --> 00:00:25.797
Skip the notes for now.

00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:29.712
Underline the goal: the action, and what it's about.

00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:31.572
Turn it into a checklist.

00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:34.742
Then pick the one choice that ticks every box.

00:00:34.742 --> 00:00:35.962
You barely need the notes.

00:00:37.043 --> 00:00:38.713
Know your goal words.

00:00:38.713 --> 00:00:42.648
A similarity needs both items, and what they share.

00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:46.258
A difference needs both items, and how they differ.

00:00:46.258 --> 00:00:51.248
For an unfamiliar audience, the answer must explain the unfamiliar thing.

00:00:51.248 --> 00:00:56.208
And aim means why, method means how, and finding means what they found.

00:00:57.226 --> 00:00:58.696
Let's try one.

00:00:58.696 --> 00:01:00.696
First, read the goal.

00:01:00.696 --> 00:01:04.816
The student wants to emphasize a difference in the lengths of the two spans.

00:01:04.816 --> 00:01:09.226
So the checklist is: two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:11.466
Choice A states a similarity.

00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:15.326
Choice B gives a difference, but in dates, not length.

00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:18.151
Choice D only mentions one bridge.

00:01:18.151 --> 00:01:22.036
Choice C has two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:01:22.036 --> 00:01:23.230
It ticks every box.

00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:27.676
Watch out for the true sentence that does a different job.

00:01:27.676 --> 00:01:29.681
Every choice is accurate.

00:01:29.681 --> 00:01:30.997
Only one hits the goal.

00:01:32.048 --> 00:01:38.893
Here's the whole lesson on one page: how to spot it, the four steps, the goal words, and the trap.

00:01:38.893 --> 00:01:41.782
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
